ROLE: systems_reviewer  VOTE: yellow
EXISTING_IMPLEMENTATIONS: [
  {system: "TensorRT-LLM priority KV retention", url: "https://nvidia.github.io/TensorRT-LLM/latest/features/kvcache.html", overlap: "High infrastructure overlap: ships token-range priority/duration retention plus prioritized LRU; proposed predictor could map tool-result spans onto this API, but TRT-LLM does not supply future-reference/tool-handle scoring."},
  {system: "H2O", url: "https://github.com/FMInference/H2O", overlap: "Direct baseline: heavy-hitter attention KV eviction retaining recent + high accumulated-attention tokens."},
  {system: "SnapKV", url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/2404.14469", overlap: "Direct baseline: attention-observation-window KV compression; reports 3.6x generation speed and 8.2x memory efficiency at 16K tokens."},
  {system: "Scissorhands", url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.17118", overlap: "Direct prior framing: persistence-of-importance hypothesis for KV cache compression; proposed delayed cold-then-hot callbacks are a counter-regime, not yet shown in real traces."},
  {system: "ACON", url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.00615", overlap: "Closest agent-domain competitor: long-horizon agent context compression on AppWorld/OfficeBench/Multi-objective QA, reports 26-54% peak token reduction; not KV eviction or this exact future-reference scorer."},
  {system: "vLLM Automatic Prefix Caching", url: "https://docs.vllm.ai/en/latest/design/prefix_caching/", overlap: "Low/medium systems overlap: shipping hash-block prefix reuse with free-queue/LRU-style eviction; no semantic tool-result future-reference retention."},
  {system: "SGLang RadixAttention", url: "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang", overlap: "Low/medium systems overlap: prefix/radix cache reuse and cache-aware serving, not per-span delayed-reference prediction."},
  {system: "LMCache", url: "https://github.com/LMCache/LMCache", overlap: "Low/medium systems overlap: reusable-text KV cache across GPU/CPU/disk/S3 with vLLM/SGLang integration; not selecting committed tool-result spans by predicted future use."},
  {system: "FlashInfer", url: "https://github.com/flashinfer-ai/flashinfer", overlap: "Low: kernels for paged/ragged KV cache, cascade/sparse attention, decode/prefill; no retention policy mechanism."}
]
CONTRIBUTION_TYPE: mechanism
SCALE_REALISM: insufficient evidence for realistic workload. The L0 is reproducible CPU simulation (`python3 sim.py && python3 analyze.py`, 64 seeds, 6400 rows) and appears to fix the prior circularity/baseline defects within that simulator, but it does not establish real tool-agent traces contain enough delayed cold-then-hot callbacks, does not use real model attention/KV behavior, and reports synthetic task-chain availability rather than end-to-end task success at GPU serving scale.
RATIONALE: PROMPT_VERSION v001. This is not killed by an exact shipping implementation: I found retention infrastructure (TensorRT-LLM token-range priority retention) and direct attention/KV baselines (H2O/SnapKV/Scissorhands), but not a shipped system that predicts delayed tool-result re-reference from noisy handle/ngram plus past-attention signals. However, the systems contribution is bounded: once a predictor exists, deployment largely maps scores to already-shipped priority-retention APIs, and the packet’s own evidence says CAUSAL ties H2O on aggregate availability, wins only on M2 where H2O/RT are 0, and loses/ties at tight budgets or crit_AUC≈0.588. Required next evidence: real LLM accumulated attention, real measured future-reference AUC on committed tool outputs, real AppWorld/OfficeBench/tau-bench-style task accuracy at matched KV/token budgets, and head-to-head against H2O/SnapKV/Scissorhands/ACON using a GPU artifact.
